Thanks for this fix! Two data points from a reproducer (ux-twig-component 3.6.0, FrankenPHP worker mode) that may help:

1. **An exception in the body of an embedded component is a more common trigger.** The code compiled by `ComponentNode` calls `startEmbedComponent()`, renders the body, then `finishEmbedComponent()` without `try/finally`. Any exception inside `<twig:X>...</twig:X>` (e.g. an `include()` of a missing template) leaves the component on the stack.
2. **It can leak data between users through `inject()`.** `ComponentRuntime::inject()` walks the stack, so a component left there provides its `provide()` values to later requests: with `AccountPanel` doing `provide('account', account)` and a top-level `<twig:Avatar />` doing `inject('account', 'guest')`, user B's page shows user A's account after A's page failed inside the panel.

I applied the `src/` parts of this PR separately to check which one covers this case:

| Applied | User B's page |
|---|---|
| nothing | `alice` ❌ |
| only the `try/catch` around `preRender()` (`ComponentRenderer.php`) | `alice` ❌ |
| only `ComponentStack::reset()` + the `kernel.reset` tag | `guest` ✅ |

So the `kernel.reset` part is what fixes it across requests in worker mode.

Found with [igor-php](https://github.com/igor-php/igor-php).
